        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(cron): add restart catch-up coverage for recurring command jobs",
        "body": "What Problem This Solves\r\nIssue #104412 reports that recurring cron jobs with payload.kind=\"command\" are silently skipped across gateway stop/start windows. ClawSweeper identified a test coverage gap: the restart catch-up suite only covered systemEvent jobs, leaving both command job recovery paths untested.\r\n\r\nWhy This Change Was Made\r\nWithout test coverage for command jobs in startup catch-up, there was no way to confirm the two recovery scenarios worked correctly:\r\n\r\nA job added but never run (no lastRunAtMs) whose nextRunAtMs falls inside a stop window\r\nA job whose nextRunAtMs was already advanced past a missed slot, requiring the allowCronMissedRunByLastRun fallback path\r\nBoth scenarios needed coverage regardless of whether a production bug exists on current main.\r\n\r\nUser Impact\r\nNo behavior change. Tests only. Proves the restart catch-up machinery correctly handles recurring command jobs in both recovery paths on current main, closing the gap ClawSweeper flagged.\r\n\r\nEvidence\r\nBoth new tests pass on current main (17/17 total in the suite):\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1043\" height=\"662\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/72f89921-b371-4a86-82e7-83506b214ccb\" />\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/cron-command-job-restart-catchup-coverage",
